  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound 5,7-dihydroxy-2-[4-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyphenyl]chromen-4-one and Leukocyte antigen CD37. This compound is implicated in targeting Melanocyte protein PMEL, which is a known target of rapamycin. Rapamycin, in turn, has a target of Leukocyte antigen CD37, indicating a possible pathway through which the compound may influence CD37. Additionally, the compound is also linked to targeting another compound, Methyl 2-[(3R,4R,6S)-4-Ethyl-6-[(2S)-2-Ethylhexyl]-6-Methyldioxan-3-Yl]Acetate, which also targets CD37. These findings suggest that the compound may act through a series of downstream pathways, ultimately affecting CD37. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
